# Resources for Language Learning AI Project

## Research Papers

1. "Deep Speech 2: End-to-End Speech Recognition in English and Mandarin"
   - Link: https://arxiv.org/abs/1512.02595
   - Relevance: Provides insights into advanced speech recognition techniques

2. "Automatic Pronunciation Assessment for Language Learning"
   - Link: https://www.isca-speech.org/archive/interspeech_2015/papers/i15_1140.pdf
   - Relevance: Discusses methods for assessing pronunciation in language learning contexts

3. "Neural Network Models for Paraphrase Identification, Semantic Textual Similarity, Natural Language Inference, and Question Answering"
   - Link: https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.04330
   - Relevance: Covers NLP techniques useful for analyzing learner responses

4. "Feedback in Intelligent Computer-Assisted Language Learning and Second Language Acquisition: A study of its effect on the acquisition of French past tense aspect"
   - Link: https://www.jstor.org/stable/44488270
   - Relevance: Discusses the importance of feedback in language learning systems

## GitHub Repositories

1. DeepSpeech
   - Link: https://github.com/mozilla/DeepSpeech
   - Description: Mozilla's open-source speech-to-text engine

2. spaCy
   - Link: https://github.com/explosion/spaCy
   - Description: Industrial-strength Natural Language Processing in Python

3. Pronunciation Evaluation
   - Link: https://github.com/suezhu/pronunciation_evaluation
   - Description: A project for evaluating English pronunciation

4. React Speech Recognition
   - Link: https://github.com/JamesBrill/react-speech-recognition
   - Description: Speech recognition for React applications

5. NLTK (Natural Language Toolkit)
   - Link: https://github.com/nltk/nltk
   - Description: Suite of libraries and programs for natural language processing

